{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"advisory":[{"agreement":1,"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Add a CLI test that drives `fsck_cli(['--repair','--only=stale-channel'])` against a real stale-channel ticket (without stubbing `_repair_run`) and asserts the only-mode report/selection, proving the parsed `only` value reaches the driver.","criteria":["tests"],"decision":"advisory","evidence":["`monkeypatch.setattr(fsck, \"_repair_run\", lambda *_args, **_kwargs: ([\"repair ran\"], 0))` — the stub discards args, so `only=\"stale-channel\"` reaching `_repair_run` is never verified","fsck.py:527 `repair_lines, _unresolved = _repair_run(tracker, dry_run=dry_run, limit=limit, repo_root=repo_root, only=only)` — the forward under test","ABSENCE: no test drives fsck_cli(['--repair','--only=stale-channel']) against a real stale-channel ticket and asserts only-mode selection (stale rebuilt, orphan/inconsistent tickets excluded, ensure sweep skipped) through the real _repair_run"],"finding":"The CLI-to-driver wiring that forwards the parsed `--only` value into `_repair_run(only=only)` (fsck.py:527) is never exercised end-to-end. The only `fsck_cli([\"--repair\", \"--only=stale-channel\"])` test stubs `_repair_run` with `lambda *_args, **_kwargs` (heldout line 72) that swallows and never asserts the `only` kwarg, and also stubs `_scan`; all positive selection/rebuild assertions call `_repair_run`/`_repair_ticket` directly. A regression dropping the `only` forward (passing None) would run the broad repair path + ensure sweep against a stale-channel-only ticket and no test would fail.","id":"0","impact":0.3,"location":"tests/interfaces/store/test_fsck_stale_channel_repair_heldout.py:70","norm_id":"n36c4d66df56ff97a","priority":0.3,"reason":"default-advisory","reviewer_id":"code-review-tests","reviewers":["code-review-tests"],"scenarios":[],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"Add an end-to-end fsck_cli test with a real seeded stale-channel ticket (and a co-located orphan/inconsistent ticket) that does NOT monkeypatch `_repair_run`; assert the stale ticket's report line appears, the other-fault ticket is excluded, and no ensure-sweep line is emitted — so a dropped `only=only` forward at fsck.py:527 fails.","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","respects_artifact_altitude":"na","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"blast_radius":"module","capability_degraded":false,"churn90":0,"contract_drift":false,"data_loss_without_recovery":false,"dead_code":false,"debt_impact":"medium","escapes_automation":true,"hard_to_reverse_surface":false,"hidden_invariant":false,"implicit_coupling":false,"likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"low","reachable_path_without_automated_coverage":true,"reversibility":"easy","safety_net_removal_without_replacement":false,"security_bypass_not_enforced_elsewhere":false,"silent_failure":true,"silent_wrong_feeding_a_decision":false,"trigger_likelihood":"rare","unversioned_published_contract_break":false}}}],"blocking":[],"change_fingerprint":"","change_id":"","coaching":[],"coverage":{"llm_ran":true,"metrics":{"cache_read_tokens":852596,"cache_write_tokens":115716,"findings_per_run":1,"grounding_health":"ok","input_tokens":978944,"llm_calls":8,"llm_ms":344539.5,"output_tokens":9219,"total_ms":522986.1,"total_tokens":988163,"verify_requests":3},"outcome_counts":{"clean